    {
      "id": "F",
      "track": "section-b",
      "printedRef": "Section B Q3 F",
      "title": "Section B Q3 F",
      "prompt": {
        "en": "If we add all of its digits for a certain positive integer, we could get a new positive integer. This procedure could be repeated, until the final result has only one digit.\n\nFor example, 1234 would produce a new integer 10 (1+2+3+4), and finally 1 (1+0). Janet wants to write a program to input a 5-digit positive integer less than 32768, and output the final single digit after performing the above-mentioned procedure.\n\nHere is her code:\n\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\nint x;\nint main(){\n  scanf(\"%d\",&x);\n  printf(\"%d\", x-(x+1)/9*9);\n}\n```\n\nHowever, she realizes that her program does not work for some cases.\nHelp Janet write down in F a counter-example which is within the input range."
      },
      "points": 3,
      "blanks": [
        {
          "id": "F",
          "label": "F",
          "maxChars": 5
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "paperUrl": "https://assets.hkoi.org/ref/2012hse.pdf",
        "answerSheetUrl": "https://assets.hkoi.org/ref/2012hsa.pdf",
        "page": 9
      },
      "grading": {
        "kind": "pending",
        "reason": "Requires the printed two-tier 2/3-mark scoring rubric for any correct counter-example versus the maximum counter-example; v1 grading is pass/fail only.",
        "intendedEngine": "c"
      }
    },
